{
  "$comment": "Shared advideo taxonomy. Single source of truth for the Python pipeline (M1) and the .NET ad matcher (M2). Edit here only. clipSceneLabels (scored with a separate softmax per kind: action / scene / object): Labels with neutral=true are distractors (never emitted): CLIP zero-shot always distributes probability over this closed set, so ordinary scenes need somewhere to go (otherwise a crowd becomes 'dancing', a screen 'gaming'). brands[].clipPrompts + clipBrandNeutral: CLIP zero-shot logo detection (softmax over brand prompts + neutral distractors, on frame crops). kind=safety labels (own softmax with everyday-scene neutrals) map to category 'sensitive' + subtype; the ad server shows no ad in sensitive segments unless platform.brandSafety.allowSensitive.",
